help mtefeplot{r})}
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Title

    mtefeplot --
                Plot MTE graphs from mtefe estimates


Syntax

        mtefeplot [namelist] , [options]

    options                    Description
    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    cropfigure(numlist)        crops the confidence bands at the min and max specified in
                                 numlist
    memory                     specifies that the estimates be restored from memory rather
                                 than disk
    normalci                   uses normal-based confidence interval rather than
                                 percentile-based for bootstrapped estimates.
    folder(string)             uses estimates saved in the subfolder string
    names(namelist)            names the plots in the legend using the names in namelist
    graph_opts(string)          add twoway options to the graph, see twoway_options
    legendtitle(string)        uses the title string for the legend
    level(#)                   plots a #% confidence interval. Default: 95%
    late                       plots the MTE for the compliers and the LATE weights
    att                        plots the MTE for the treated and the ATT weights
    atut                       plots the MTE for the untreated and the ATUT weights
    prte                       plots the MTE for the policy compliers and the PRTE weights
    mprte1                     plots the weights for the Marginal Policy Relevant Treatment
                                 Effect 1
    mprte2                     plots the weights for the Marginal Policy Relevant Treatment
                                 Effect 2
    mprte3                     plots the weights for the Marginal Policy Relevant Treatment
                                 Effect 3
    separate                   plots the estimated outcomes separately for the treated and
                                 untreated state
    trimsupport                only plots the MTE for unobserved resistance between the two
                                 values in trimsupport
    points                     use scatter rather than line plots for the MTE(s), useful when
                                 support is limited.

    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description

    mtefeplot plots the marginal treatment effects from previously stored or saved estimates
    from mtefe.

    If namelist is empty or contains one name and neither options late, att, atut or prte is
    specified, mtefeplot will plot a standard Marginal Treatment effects plot of the stored
    or saved estimate. If it contains estimates of the standard errors, confidence bands are
    included.  Graph includes a plot of the average treatment effect for reference. If
    namelist is empty, estimates from memory is used.

    If namelist is empty or contains one name, separate is specified and no treatment
    parameter options are specified, mtefeplot will plot the outcomes in the treated and
    untreated state separately together with the MTE curve. Average treatment effect is
    plotted for reference.

    If namelist contains more than two names, mtefeplot plots several MTE plots in the same
    graphs with no confidence bands.

    If namelist is empty or contains one name, and either late, att ,atut, prte, mprte1,
    mprte2 or mprte3 is specified, mtefeplot plots treatment parameter graphs. These contain
    a) the MTE for the particular treatment effect requested, b) the estimated weights over
    the U_d distribution for the requested treatment effect parameter and c) the point
    estimate of the treatment effect labeled at the left axis. In addition, the main MTE
    graph and the average treatment effect is plotted for reference. If late is specified,
    the regular 2SLS estimate is also dotted for reference.  If namelist is empty, estimates
    from memory is used. More than two treatment effect parameters specified at the same time
    will clutter the figure, and is not recommended.

    More than two names in namelist and either treatment parameter option or the separate
    option gives an error.


Examples

    Generate some data and estimate MTE
        . mtefe_gendata
        . mtefe lwage exp exp2 (col=distCol)
        . est sto normal
        . mtefe lwage exp exp2 (col=distCol), separate pol(2)
        . est sto polynomial
        . est save myfolder/polynomial
        . mtefe lwage exp exp2 (col=distCol), semiparametric gridponts(100)
        . est sto semipar

    Standard MTE plot of the estimate in memory
        . mtefeplot

    Plots of three different saved MTE estimates in the same graph
        . mtefeplot normal polynomial semipar, memory legendtitle("Specification")
            names("Normal" "Polynomial" "Semiparametric")

    Plot of the estimated local average treatment effect and weights
        . mtefeplot normal, mem late

    Plot of the estimated ATT and ATUT with weights
        . mtefeplot polynomial, mem att atut

    Plot of outcomes in the treated and untreated state of an estimate saved in "myfolder"
        . mtefeplot polynomial, folder(myfolder) separate

Author

    Martin Eckhoff Andresen
    University of Oslo & Statistics Norway
    Oslo, NO
    martin.eckhoff.andresen@gmail.com

Also see
       Main help file for mtefe

. 
